  "diagnosis": "The flexed ramp reaches its geometry. After 163 commands all eight joints sit within 8 mrad of the calculated targets (hips -0.32 rad, knees +0.68 rad), the torso is 15 mm lower and 70 mm further forward than at entry, and every leg's zero-bias reference path is feasible at the final sample. Rear-right bore no load for the first 55 ramp samples; from sample 60 through the end of the ramp all four feet bore load. After the ramp the fixed-joint hold never settles: 5 of 240 samples are ready (indices 73, 74, 187, 188, 196), never 30 consecutive. Post-ramp horizontal COM speed spans 0.004 to 0.162 m/s with mean 0.075 m/s against the 0.03 m/s limit, angular speed spikes to 0.50 rad/s, torso x oscillates over 10 mm, 32 post-ramp samples lose bearing on one foot (front-left 18), and measured joint velocities spike to 1.6 rad/s under the shared 8/s gain, 0.65 damping law with its 0.75 rad/s clamp. The motion is not decaying, so a longer dwell alone is unsupported by this data. The kicked role passes the measured entry check at step 858 and unchanged V50 completes four planned cycles, the 1037-command cycle end, the 120-command stop and 0.1197974943 m forward advance at 2015 solver steps, with a finite measurement identical to the R10H kicked child. This supports replacing the post-ramp fixed-joint dwell, not the ramp geometry, the kicked route, or V50 walking.",
